  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "note-found",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "The system every screen is built from.\nOne rule drives all of it: a missed day must never look like failure — there is no red anywhere for an\nabsence, and the headline number is always 30-day consistency, never the streak."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-start",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -170,
      "w": 880,
      "text": "Onboarding does one unusual thing: it argues you DOWN to two habits, and it treats finding a group\nas a required step rather than an upsell. Both are lifted straight from the retention research."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-day",
      "page": "page-3",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -170,
      "w": 880,
      "text": "The daily loop, and what happens at its edges.\nThe three sheets are the log flows — amount, timer, and the skip flow that protects the streak.\nSkip is a first-class state, not a null."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-habit",
      "page": "page-4",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 880,
      "text": "Detail, creation and editing — including a breaking habit, which reads and scores differently\nfrom a building one."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-group",
      "page": "page-5",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 880,
      "text": "The accountability layer. Note what is absent: no leaderboard by default, no downvote,\nand nudges rate-limited to once a week per person."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-you",
      "page": "page-6",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -170,
      "w": 880,
      "text": "Account, the notification budget, and the lapse screen — the one no competitor has.\nSystem states last: a habit tracker that loses an entry is worse than no habit tracker,\nso every failure state says where the data actually is."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-desk",
      "page": "page-7",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "Same data at desktop width. The per-habit week strip and the full-year heatmap are the two things\na phone genuinely cannot show."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-dir",
      "page": "page-8",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 880,
      "text": "Two directions I did not take, kept so you can push back. Each names its own trade-off."
    }
  ],
  "launch": {
    "view": "canvas",
    "page": "page-3"
  }
}